    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Search and download materials (stickers, audio, ...) from the Jianying/Capcut\r\nplatform.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  search                                Search assets by type and natural-language intent.\r\n  download                              Download an asset file by type and resource ID.\r\n  query                                 Inspect metadata for a known material resource ID.\r\n  topic                                 Browse material topic collections, or list assets inside a\r\n                                        specific topic.\r\n  recommend                             Fetch a recommended / hot material list for the given asset type.\r\n                                        (WIP)\r\n  similar                               Fetch similar materials seeded by an existing resource ID. (WIP)\r\n  motiongraph                           MotionGraph runtime-data generation (phase-2 downsink of the\r\n                                        stylecut consumer orchestration).\r\n\r\nWORKFLOW\r\n  Find resource_id through either discovery path:\r\n\r\n  Search by intent\r\n     material search   --type <asset_type> --prompt \"<intent>\"\r\n\r\n  Browse curated pools\r\n     material topic    --type <asset_type>\r\n     material topic    --type <asset_type> --id <topic_id>\r\n\r\n  Use resource_id after a candidate is selected:\r\n\r\n  Inspect metadata\r\n     material query    --resource-id <id>\r\n\r\n  Download asset\r\n     material download --type <asset_type> --resource-id <id>\r\n\r\nCOMMON ASSET TYPES (examples)\r\n  template, music, sticker, effect, filter, transition, text_template, sound, photo, video\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search   --type sticker --prompt \"cute cat\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search   --type music --prompt \"warm acoustic vlog\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli material topic    --type sticker\r\n  $ lyra-cli material topic    --type sticker --id 123 --limit 10\r\n  $ lyra-cli material query    --resource-id \"7586591573920664856\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli material download --type sticker --resource-id \"7586591573920664856\"\r\n\r\nHELP\r\n  Use `lyra-cli material <command> --help` for command-specific guidance.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Search and download materials (stickers, audio, ...) from the Jianying/Capcut\r\nplatform.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  search                                Search assets by type and natural-language intent.\r\n  download                              Download an asset file by type and resource ID.\r\n  query                                 Inspect metadata for a known material resource ID.\r\n  topic                                 Browse material topic collections, or list assets inside a\r\n                                        specific topic.\r\n  recommend                             Fetch a recommended / hot material list for the given asset type.\r\n                                        (WIP)\r\n  similar                               Fetch similar materials seeded by an existing resource ID. (WIP)\r\n  motiongraph                           MotionGraph runtime-data generation (phase-2 downsink of the\r\n                                        stylecut consumer orchestration).\r\n\r\nWORKFLOW\r\n  Find resource_id through either discovery path:\r\n\r\n  Search by intent\r\n     material search   --type <asset_type> --prompt \"<intent>\"\r\n\r\n  Browse curated pools\r\n     material topic    --type <asset_type>\r\n     material topic    --type <asset_type> --id <topic_id>\r\n\r\n  Use resource_id after a candidate is selected:\r\n\r\n  Inspect metadata\r\n     material query    --resource-id <id>\r\n\r\n  Download asset\r\n     material download --type <asset_type> --resource-id <id>\r\n\r\nCOMMON ASSET TYPES (examples)\r\n  template, music, sticker, effect, filter, transition, text_template, sound, photo, video\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search   --type sticker --prompt \"cute cat\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli material search   --type music --prompt \"warm acoustic vlog\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli material topic    --type sticker\r\n  $ lyra-cli material topic    --type sticker --id 123 --limit 10\r\n  $ lyra-cli material query    --resource-id \"7586591573920664856\"\r\n  $ lyra-cli material download --type sticker --resource-id \"7586591573920664856\"\r\n\r\nHELP\r\n  Use `lyra-cli material <command> --help` for command-specific guidance.\r\n",
